      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{59cb4676d4edc012b9dca22f|full_name}: According to Unity a 2048x2048 (max mirror resolution) render texture is 32 MB for RGBA32, and 48 MB for a ARGB Half. This isn't going to make a difference, and based on what Merlin has said below, Unity's already using an ARGB Half internally anyways so getting rid of the RGBA32 texture should be a net savings.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
